.TH KEWSTATERC 5 "2026-09-24" "kew" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
kewstaterc \- persisted runtime state file for kew
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/kew/kewstaterc
.RB ( Linux / FreeBSD / Android ),
.I ~/Library/Preferences/kew/kewstaterc
.RB ( macOS )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kewstaterc
stores settings that
.BR kew (1)
changes automatically at runtime as the user interacts with the
application, such as toggling notifications or adjusting the volume.
It uses the same INI-style syntax as
.BR kewrc (5):
named sections in square brackets, each containing
.IR key = value
pairs.
.PP
Unlike
.BR kewrc (5),
which the user is expected to hand-edit, kew writes to
.B kewstaterc
itself whenever the corresponding in-app setting changes. Values in
.B kewstaterc
take precedence over the same-named keys in
.BR kewrc (5),
so a setting changed from within kew will override its
.B kewrc
value on subsequent runs.
.PP
If
.B kewstaterc
is deleted, kew regenerates it with default values the next time it
writes state.
.SH "MISCELLANEOUS SECTION"
Settings in the
.B [miscellaneous]
section.
.TP
.BI allowNotifications " bool"
Whether desktop notifications are enabled. Mirrors and overrides the
.B kewrc
setting of the same name. Default:
.IR 1 .
.TP
.BI alwaysCrossfade " bool"
Whether crossfade at the end of every song is enabled. Mirrors and
overrides the
.B kewrc
setting of the same name. Default:
.IR 1 .
.TP
.BI lastVolume " n"
The volume level in effect when kew was last closed, on a scale of
.IR 0 " to " 100 .
Restored on the next launch if
.B autoResume
or equivalent volume-restore behavior applies. Default:
.IR 5 .
.SH "TRACK COVER SECTION"
Settings in the
.B [track cover]
section.
.TP
.BI coverAnsi " bool"
Whether covers are rendered using ASCII/ANSI art mode. Mirrors and
overrides the
.B kewrc
setting of the same name. Default:
.IR 0 .
.SH "VISUALIZER SECTION"
Settings in the
.B [visualizer]
section.
.TP
.BI visualizerColortype " int"
The active visualizer color mode. Mirrors and overrides the
.B visualizerColorType
setting in
.BR kewrc (5).
.RS
.IP 0 4
lighten
.IP 1 4
flat
.IP 2 4
reversed lighten
.IP 3 4
party
.IP 4 4
vibrant
.IP 5 4
lum vibrant
.IP 6 4
binning
.IP 7 4
two color gradient
.IP 8 4
off
.RE
.IP
Default:
.IR 3 .
.SH "CHROMA SECTION"
Settings in the
.B [chroma]
section.
.TP
.BI chromaPreset " n"
Index of the last-selected Chroma preset. A value of
.I \-1
means no preset is selected. Default:
.IR \-1 .
.SH "COLORS SECTION"
Settings in the
.B [colors]
section.
.TP
.BI colorMode " int"
The active color palette source. Mirrors and overrides the
.B colorMode
setting in
.BR kewrc (5).
.RS
.IP 0 4
16-bit color palette from the default theme
.IP 1 4
colors derived from the One Album Color theme
.IP 2 4
colors derived from the TrueColor theme
.IP 3 4
colors derived from the Album Colors theme
.IP 4 4
neutral, devoid of color
.RE
.IP
Default:
.IR 3 .
.TP
.BI theme " name"
Name of the currently selected theme file, as found in
.I ~/.config/kew/themes
(Linux/FreeBSD/Android) or
.I ~/Library/Preferences/kew/themes
(macOS). Mirrors and overrides the
.B theme
setting in
.BR kewrc (5).
Empty selects the default theme.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kew/kewstaterc
State file on Linux, FreeBSD, and Android.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Preferences/kew/kewstaterc
State file on macOS.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR kew (1),
.BR kewrc (5)
